## Dishes

ent-WFFoodHuntersChicken = hunter's chicken
    .desc = A chicken breast wrapped in bacon, smothered in barbecue sauce and melted cheese. A pub menu staple.
ent-WFFoodBeansOnToast = beans on toast
    .desc = Baked beans heaped on buttered toast.
ent-WFFoodEtonMess = Eton mess
    .desc = Crushed meringue, whipped cream and berries in a glass.
ent-WFFoodScones = scones with jam and cream
    .desc = Two split scones loaded with jam and clotted cream.
ent-WFFoodStickyToffeePudding = sticky toffee pudding
    .desc = A moist date sponge drowned in hot toffee sauce.
ent-WFFoodMarsBarBattered = battered chocolate bar
    .desc = A chocolate bar dredged in a gloopy flour and egg batter. It wants frying.
ent-WFFoodDeepFriedMarsBar = deep fried Mars bar
    .desc = Battered, deep fried and molten in the middle, each one closes an artery a little further.
ent-WFFoodCornishPasty = Cornish pasty
    .desc = Beef, potato and onion baked in a crimped pastry case.
ent-WFFoodCheesyBeanMelt = sausage, bean and cheese melt
    .desc = Sausage, baked beans and molten cheese sealed in the sacred flaky puff pastry.
ent-WFFoodPieSteakAle = steak and ale pie
    .desc = Chunks of beef braised in dark ale and gravy under a golden pastry lid.
ent-WFFoodPieSteakAleSlice = steak and ale pie slice
    .desc = A slice of steak and ale pie. The gravy is already making a break for it.
ent-WFFoodPiePork = pork pie
    .desc = A hand-raised pie of seasoned pork set in savoury jelly. Best eaten cold, with mustard.
ent-WFFoodPiePorkSlice = pork pie quarter
    .desc = A quarter of a pork pie. The jelly is load-bearing.
ent-WFFoodPieChickenMushroom = chicken and mushroom pie
    .desc = A small pie of chicken and mushrooms in a thick, creamy sauce.
ent-WFFoodPieChickenMushroomSlice = chicken and mushroom pie quarter
    .desc = A quarter of a chicken and mushroom pie, creamy filling and all.
ent-WFFoodSoupWelshCawl = Welsh cawl
    .desc = A slow-simmered broth of lamb, leek, potato and carrot. A Welsh classic, and better the day after.

## Mrs. Luvvit's packs and what comes out of them

ent-WFFoodPackHuntersChicken = hunter's chicken ready meal
    .desc = Hunter's chicken in a plastic tray under clear film. The barbecue sauce has already claimed the corners.
ent-WFFoodPackSteakAlePie = packaged steak and ale pie
    .desc = A whole steak and ale pie in a tray, sleeved in card. Serves five, or one very determined spacer.
ent-WFFoodPackSteakAlePieSlice = packaged steak and ale pie slice
    .desc = A single slice of steak and ale pie, sealed in film. The gravy pools at the bottom.
ent-WFFoodPackPorkPie = packaged pork pie
    .desc = A pork pie in a paper case. The label promises real pork.
ent-WFFoodPackChickenMushroomPie = packaged chicken and mushroom pie
    .desc = A chicken and mushroom pie in a paper case. Somewhere in there, a mushroom.
ent-WFFoodPackCornishPasty = wrapped Cornish pasty
    .desc = A Cornish pasty in a foil-lined paper sleeve. The crimping is suspiciously even.
ent-WFFoodPackWelshCawl = Welsh cawl pouch
    .desc = Welsh cawl in a pouch you eat straight from. Mostly broth, with the odd lump of lamb.
ent-WFFoodPackCheesyBeanMelt = bagged sausage, bean and cheese melt
    .desc = A sausage, bean and cheese melt in a paper bag.
ent-WFFoodPackEtonMess = Eton mess pot
    .desc = A plastic pot of Eton mess under a peel-off foil lid.
ent-WFFoodPackScones = boxed scones
    .desc = Two scones in a carton topped with jam and cream.
ent-WFFoodPackStickyToffeePudding = sticky toffee pudding tub
    .desc = A sealed tub of sticky toffee pudding, the sauce already soaking in.
