## Empty containers

ent-WFTrashPackHuntersChicken = empty ready meal tray
    .desc = A plastic tray with a smear of barbecue sauce and a couple of cheese crumbs.
ent-WFTrashPackSteakAlePie = empty pie tray
    .desc = A foil pie tray with a gravy stain and a scatter of pastry crumbs.
ent-WFTrashPackSteakAlePieSlice = empty pie slice tray
    .desc = A small tray with a smear of gravy, bits of beef and flakes of pastry where a slice of pie used to be.
ent-WFTrashPackPorkPie = empty pork pie case
    .desc = A crumpled paper pie case. A few crumbs of pastry and jelly cling to it.
ent-WFTrashPackChickenMushroomPie = empty chicken and mushroom pie case
    .desc = A crumpled paper pie case with a streak of cream sauce down one side.
ent-WFTrashPackCornishPasty = empty pasty sleeve
    .desc = A torn, foil-lined paper sleeve with pastry crumbs in the bottom.
ent-WFTrashPackWelshCawl = empty soup pouch
    .desc = A deflated soup pouch. The last dribble of broth refuses to come out.
ent-WFTrashPackEtonMess = empty dessert pot
    .desc = A plastic pot smeared with cream and berry, its foil lid peeled back.
ent-WFTrashPackScones = empty scone carton
    .desc = A carton with a crumpled paper liner, smeared with jam and cream.
ent-WFTrashPackStickyToffeePudding = empty pudding tub
    .desc = A black tub with a puddle of toffee sauce in one corner.
ent-WFTrashPackCheesyBeanMelt = greasy paper bag
    .desc = A crumpled paper bag with a grease spot.

## Drinks

ent-WFDrinkIrnBruCan = Irn-Bru can
    .desc = A luminous orange soda. Nobody has ever managed to name the flavour.
ent-WFDrinkDandelionBurdockCan = dandelion and burdock can
    .desc = A dark, fizzy root soda, sweet and herbal.

